      "number": 1,
      "status": "accepted",
      "explanation": "Replace the list\u2011based elimination with a classic Eratosthenes sieve using a contiguous boolean array. The original algorithm repeatedly scans and erases elements from a std::list, giving O(N^2) behaviour and many heap allocations. By computing the maximum value once, allocating a vector<char> of that size, marking non\u2011primes in O(N log log N) time and then copying the remaining primes into the output vector, we keep the same observable result (the count of primes) while dramatically reducing work. The function also clears the input list to preserve the side\u2011effect that the original code empties it. Adding <algorithm> provides max_element used for the bound.",
      "model_call": {
